.TH SDL_GetWindowSize 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetWindowSize \- Get the size of a window\(aqs client area.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetWindowSize(SDL_Window *window, int *w, int *h);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The window pixel size may differ from its window coordinate size if the window is on a high pixel density display\[char46] Use
.BR SDL_GetWindowSizeInPixels ()
or
.BR SDL_GetRenderOutputSize ()
to get the real client area size in pixels\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to query the width and height from\[char46]
.TP
.I w
a pointer filled in with the width of the window, may be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I h
a pointer filled in with the height of the window, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetRenderOutputSize (3),
.BR SDL_GetWindowSizeInPixels (3),
.BR SDL_SetWindowSize (3),
